So we find the dreamer in a desolate split world in which there's only one being, but it is split off far away in the distance, too far to reach, standing helpless in a situation of introversion, unable to move forward or backward. The important thing here is really the splitting of the soul.

00:36:55.380 --> 00:37:13.473
Jung sees it that when things are in the unconscious, So below our level of consciousness, they kind of disintegrate. They're not connected. A little bit like the Tower of Babel that was one thing, but then was struck and things multiplied and broke apart.

00:37:14.839 --> 00:37:34.064
He says, when we look into the psyche, we have there a rather different view. So we have in our unconscious many, many separate things. That look rather separated from each other, but can be connected in a single thing.

00:37:37.553 --> 00:37:46.475
The example that he had here for the schizophrenics, schizo and phren meaning the, the split phren, so the split mind.

00:37:49.270 --> 00:38:09.232
Jung would say that they would encounter multiples of, for example, insects or animals, or yeah, animals that would show this split of the mind, the splitting apart of a unifying idea into many, many different things.

00:38:10.068 --> 00:38:22.327
So when you dream of multiple things of the same thing, they're still somehow related, even though that they look separated. Okay, this sounds now very complicated. But I have a better example for that.

00:38:25.360 --> 00:38:47.306
You might be familiar with a lot of imagery of the gate where you often have like two guardians guarding a kind of threshold to another realm. So you have one statue or multiple statues. For example, in The Neverending Story, you have these gate of the two sphinxes that kill anything that's not pure of heart when it goes through.

00:38:49.940 --> 00:39:14.083
And you have this also, for example, on the tarot card of the Moon, where you have the kind of dualities of, of the two towers that open up the, the unknown world. But also you have the, the wolf and the dog as a multitude of the same thing, but facets of the same thing. And this is also why it's always difficult to talk about symbology.

00:39:16.250 --> 00:39:43.132
But I hope it's a little bit clear what Jung means when there should be paid special attention to how things are split up or numbered in Dreams or in Motives or in Imagery, because this very often means that things are separated split-off unconscious, they're not yet working in a harmonious way.

00:39:45.010 --> 00:40:06.979
But Jung would go further than that again, and this is a little bit a fun thing. So this sounded all very abstractly now, but every time I think to myself, ah, what Jung talks about, it could be anything, right? You can just hypothesize a lot of things, but of it's whether it's actually happening or not. Is another thing.

00:40:08.054 --> 00:40:31.817
Until, for me at least, I hit certain experiences where I say, oh my God, basically what Jung's saying is pretty— makes a lot of sense. And I have here an example that I'm pretty proud of that I've noticed it. And he talks about numbers in an odd or even way, meaning whether they are masculine or they're feminine. In their attributes.

00:40:32.121 --> 00:40:54.325
Here it's very important to understand that masculinity and femininity does not mean male and female. We're talking about psychological forces. We're talking about symbolic forces. So masculine as the active, feminine as the receptive and resting, let's say. And you think like, yeah, okay, could be, could be anything.

00:40:54.517 --> 00:41:18.502
But at the same time, when we look how we use symbols. When we have— want to have something move, we have a triangle with 3 corners, which is an odd number, which brings movement, and this is symbolized— symbolically associated with active, striving, masculine forces.

00:41:20.213 --> 00:41:43.463
And if we want things to rest, We have the symbol with the four corners that says like, stop anything that's happening now. We're now rest. Now it's harmonious, complete, stop. And this is how we have the play button and the stop button. And we have that in almost every app. And we don't really think about it, why it is like that.

00:41:43.624 --> 00:41:54.582
And I look at this and say, oh, well, basically like from a symbolical point of view, that kind of makes sense. And then it goes even further.

00:41:55.810 --> 00:42:14.127
For all the people who are living in Berlin and are familiar with the Berlin trains, we have a very big ring around like the center of Berlin that is 36, 37 kilometers, and we have two trains running in opposite directions called the Ringbahn. The ring train.

00:42:15.720 --> 00:42:34.296
And here again, it is funny how symbolically things moving to the right are masculine, moving into consciousness, and things moving left go in the unconscious, like feminine.

00:42:38.120 --> 00:43:02.373
And Jung saw there's similar movement and also in a funny way in the movement of the swastika of the Nazis, because the swastika is a very old symbol and it's moving in the old Indian way. It's moving to the right. It's moving into consciousness, right? And the furthering of consciousness.

00:43:03.112 --> 00:43:25.320
But the Nazis, they flipped it around that it moves to the left in the unconscious. So it becomes then very interesting that you have a regressive, back to the primitive, back to the nature movement, unconscious movement that's abandoning civilization, basically, that has a symbol that moves to the left.

00:43:26.846 --> 00:43:49.394
And I don't want to say similarly, but on a similar note in regards to movement, we have the Berlin Ringbahn. Where the one with the, the odd number, the masculine number, moves in the clockwise direction, and the one with the feminine number, the 42, moves in the counterclockwise direction.

00:43:49.972 --> 00:44:04.454
And I have to say, this is the way how I remember which one goes in which direction. Because Jung helps to understand the Berlin train system. Yeah.

00:44:04.454 --> 00:44:21.988
So these are the things that Jung talked about with numbers in regards to numbers, and I hope there were some examples here that were also easily understandable and applicable to people when they, for example, come to Berlin. I, I want to wrap this up.

00:44:22.960 --> 00:44:46.678
What I want to say and what Jung wants to say about Physics and Numbers and Psychology is that we as human beings have kind of the possibility to reach things of the outside world also through our inside perception and experience and awareness, which is possible because we are connected to the world.

00:44:46.951 --> 00:44:55.941
We are not only a mind, but we are also a body, and the both things, they're not completely separated from each other, but they're bleeding into each other. They feed on each other.

00:44:56.407 --> 00:45:16.169
And they allow us to do things that seem to be very strange and unique, as for example, physics or engineering or mathematics that allow us to influence and manipulate the world and anticipate the world in a way that is not completely self-evident.

00:45:16.313 --> 00:45:32.372
How human beings can describe and explain how the heavenly bodies and the galaxies move and they, how they behave. Things that are hundreds of billions of light years away, we can exactly say like, oh yeah, this star is built up like this and these things are moving like this.

00:45:33.578 --> 00:45:41.550
And this is an enormous, interesting psychological thing that we do not question so much, but it's amazing to think about.

00:45:42.340 --> 00:45:58.791
And what Jung would do, and this is classical Jung, he would look into all different avenues of human scientific endeavor or cultural products and try to find out more about the human psyche and how everything is connected.

00:45:59.225 --> 00:46:12.904
So also here he takes physics and tries to find things that kind of prove, not prove him right, but bring him into an, given him indication what is the right way to go to explain and experience things.

00:46:13.433 --> 00:46:37.213
This is how he then can combine physics with dream symbology or with yoga and also alchemy and hermeneutical thought. So this is Jung wandering the earth, looking at things and combining them all. And yeah, having really interesting thoughts in the process. And this was this event's topic.

00:46:37.903 --> 00:46:55.403
And I want to thank you for paying attention. Now I'm very interested in the discussion about this, yeah, strange topic of physics and numbers and psychology. So, yep. Thank you all.

